       Keep it small (WebP, under ~150 KB). -->

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>Write pages in Markdown, with a few directives for notes, steps, tabs and content that changes with the product or its version.</li>
    <li>Check every link, include, phrase and code example as you type in VS Code, and again in CI, so the docs can't quietly break.</li>
    <li>Build one set of files into a website with Astro, a plain Markdown copy of every page for AI assistants, and JSON.</li>
    <li>Review a change to the docs as the pages a reader will see, not as a diff of Markdown.</li>
    <li>Give AI coding agents the same checks, so what they write is held to the same rules as what you write.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why a small studio makes a docs tool</h2>
  <p>Documentation drifts from the software it describes, one small change at a time, and nobody notices until a reader follows it into a wall. Ascribe treats docs the way code is treated, so the drift is caught where it starts. It is grown the way everything here is: slowly, a release at a time, with care.</p>

  <h2>Get it</h2>
  <p>Ascribe has its own site, with its documentation, its install steps and its changelog.</p>
  <p><a class="button" href="https://ascribed-dev.com">Visit ascribed-dev.com</a></p>
  <ul>
    <li>The source, and every release: <a href="https://github.com/ascribed-dev/ascribe">github.com/ascribed-dev/ascribe</a></li>
    <li>The VS Code extension: <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Ascribe.ascribe-vscode">Ascribe on the Visual Studio Marketplace</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ascribe is free and open source, under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>Ascribe collects nothing. Read what it sends, when, and to whom in the <a href="/privacy/ascribe/">Ascribe privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Found a bug or have an idea? <a href="https://github.com/ascribed-dev/ascribe/issues">Open an issue on GitHub</a>, where it can be tracked. Report a security problem privately, as <a href="https://github.com/ascribed-dev/ascribe/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Ascribe's security policy</a> says. For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:hello@bryostudio.com">hello@bryostudio.com</a>.</p>
